WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:06.092
Judea and Samaria, since 7 October 2023. Attack, self-defence – or assault?

2
00:00:07.242 --> 00:00:14.321
35 Israelis were killed in attacks – shot, stabbed, run over. 19 of them were civilians.

3
00:00:15.472 --> 00:00:23.805
In the same period, 59 Palestinians died at the hands of settlers, security guards or off-duty soldiers – or so it is claimed.

4
00:00:24.955 --> 00:00:27.750
But who attacked – and who was assaulted?

5
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.382
We examined every case individually.

6
00:00:31.681 --> 00:00:34.058
Five were attackers who were stopped.

7
00:00:34.359 --> 00:00:40.054
In seven, the Israeli side speaks of an attack; the Palestinian side denies it.

8
00:00:40.353 --> 00:00:45.212
Eighteen times, stone-throwing is mentioned. Whether there was a danger to life remains open.

9
00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:50.266
Thirteen died in assaults, without any source attributing violence to them.

10
00:00:50.566 --> 00:00:54.719
And in sixteen, it is unclear whether settlers or soldiers fired.

11
00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:59.266
Since then, only a single Israeli has been indicted for a killing.

12
00:00:59.566 --> 00:01:05.888
And according to Yesh Din, over 93 per cent of investigations against Israeli civilians end without an indictment.

13
00:01:07.037 --> 00:01:11.661
The army counts far fewer Palestinian attacks than in 2023.

14
00:01:11.961 --> 00:01:17.499
But more settler violence: up 63 per cent in the first half of 2026.

15
00:01:18.649 --> 00:01:22.280
37 of the 51 cases are confirmed by the Israeli side.

16
00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:27.334
All cases, both accounts: biest.com/js.
